{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents. Further node inputs can be added before awaiting the answer.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct NodePhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.NodePhase` is a marker type. Its text has two obligations: (1) it marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents, and (2) further node inputs can be added before awaiting the answer. The type is a unit struct, so it has no validation or serialized form to test.\n\n**Obligation 1: the node-phase marker.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` calls `ctx.ask::<Answer>().context(..).contents_of_current_node()`. That call returns an `Ask<.., NodePhase>`, since the implementations in `src/procedure.rs` give `contents_of_current_node`, `contents_of_node` and `contents_of_successors` that return type. The test then awaits the resulting request, which only compiles if the node-phase request is awaitable.\n\n**Obligation 2: further inputs before awaiting.** The same test chains `contents_of_successors(7)` and a second `contents_of_current_node()` onto the already-started node-phase request before `.into_future()`. It asserts the following:\n- The agent receives the inputs in order, with repetition: 1, 3, 2, 3, 1.\n- The graph reads happen as `[1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`.\n- The dependency snapshots are recorded.\n- The future is `Send`.\n\nThis would fail if node-phase requests could not accept more node inputs, or if they dropped or reordered them.\n\n**Supporting tests.**\n- `task_messages_share_a_prefix_and_can_queue_another_node` is not marked as a `NodePhase` test. It also explicitly names `Ask<.., NodePhase>` and awaits it, which gives extra coverage but is not needed for the verdict.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that the public `NodePhase` struct is exported as the appendix specifies.\n\nThe phase restriction (`context` is not available after the node phase) is enforced by the type system and belongs to `judge.phases`, not to this requirement. The marker declaration also carries a compile-fail doctest for it.\n\nI found no obligation that is untested, and no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "909f09d5168c839a764d052216fd8a81d52222d7dce5a9a991746bb17ad69803",
